       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 600 mg once daily is three times the maximum labeled sertraline dose for adults, which is 200 mg/day. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and severe GI or bleeding effects. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **50 mg once daily**, the usual starting dose for depression, GAD, and similar conditions\n- **100 mg or 150 mg once daily**, a typical titrated dose\n- **200 mg once daily**, the maximum dose\n- **A different dose or drug**, if there was a typo or mix-up (for example, 600 mg is a normal dose for other medications)\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 600 mg, for example under a specialist protocol, tell me that and give me the rationale. I'd want that documented in the order note, and I'd suggest confirming it with pharmacy first."
      }
